From: Claude (odroid-m1-bsp-kernel session)
Subject: [PATCH] video/wayland: request EGL_PLATFORM_WAYLAND_KHR explicitly

Wayland_GLES_LoadLibrary() calls SDL_EGL_LoadLibrary() with platform=0,
which skips the entire SDL_VIDEO_DRIVER_MALI-gated code path in
SDL_EGL_LoadLibrary() (src/video/SDL_egl.c) that would otherwise call
eglGetPlatformDisplayEXT(). SDL2 falls through to the plain
eglGetDisplay(native_display) instead.

On this board's Mali-G52 vendor blob, eglGetDisplay() accepts a raw
wl_display* without erroring (eglGetError() reports EGL_SUCCESS) but
the resulting display handle then fails at eglInitialize() with
EGL_NOT_INITIALIZED (0x3001) - confirmed by reproducing the exact
eglGetDisplay()+eglInitialize() call sequence standalone via ctypes
against the real device. eglGetProcAddress("eglGetPlatformDisplayEXT")
does return a valid function pointer on this blob (EGL_EXT_platform_wayland
is advertised in its client extension string, confirmed via labwc/
wlroots's own successful EGL init log), so the platform-aware path is
actually implemented and available - SDL2 just never asks for it here.

Mesa/Panfrost's eglGetDisplay() happens to accept a wl_display* natively
(a backward-compatibility courtesy many mature open source EGL
implementations add), which is why this same code works unmodified on
the shared rk3568 (mainline kernel + Panfrost) target and the gap only
shows up with this vendor blob.

--enable-video-mali is already on for this build (SDL_VIDEO_DRIVER_MALI
is defined), so no other build-time config change is needed - passing
the platform constant here is the only missing piece.

--- a/src/video/wayland/SDL_waylandopengles.c
+++ b/src/video/wayland/SDL_waylandopengles.c
@@ -37,7 +37,11 @@ int Wayland_GLES_LoadLibrary(_THIS, const char *path)
     int ret;
     SDL_VideoData *data = (SDL_VideoData *)_this->driverdata;
 
-    ret = SDL_EGL_LoadLibrary(_this, path, (NativeDisplayType) data->display, 0);
+    /* Pass EGL_PLATFORM_WAYLAND_KHR explicitly so SDL_VIDEO_DRIVER_MALI's
+     * eglGetPlatformDisplayEXT() path (SDL_EGL_LoadLibrary(), SDL_egl.c) is
+     * actually taken instead of silently falling back to eglGetDisplay(),
+     * which this board's vendor Mali blob doesn't handle for Wayland. */
+    ret = SDL_EGL_LoadLibrary(_this, path, (NativeDisplayType) data->display, EGL_PLATFORM_WAYLAND_KHR);
 
     Wayland_PumpEvents(_this);
     WAYLAND_wl_display_flush(data->display);
